Geo routing & Traffic Control
    nginx identified USER location based on IP address & route traffic

1. Basic Geo ip (manuall adding)   2. GeoIP database

1. Basic Geo ip
# Define a geo block for basic manual IP-based routing
geo $country {
    default "OTHER";
    127.0.0.1 "LOCAL";
    192.168.1.0/24 "INDIA";
}

server {
    listen 80;
    server_name geo.unemployengineer.works;

    location / {
        if ($country = "LOCAL") {
            return 200 "LOCAL";
        }

        if ($country = "INDIA") {
            return 200 "INDIA";
        }

        return 200 "HELLO WORLD";
    }
}

2. Real GeoIP database setup
# Install GeoIP module and database
# For Ubuntu/Debian:
# sudo apt-get install geoip-database libnginx-mod-http-geoip
# For CentOS/RHEL:
# sudo yum install geoip geoip-devel

# Example using GeoIP database
http {
    geoip_country /usr/share/GeoIP/GeoIP.dat;

    server {
        listen 80;
        server_name geo.unemployengineer.works;

        location / {
            set $country_code $geoip_country_code;

            if ($country_code = "US") {
                return 200 "Hello, User from the United States!";
            }
            if ($country_code = "IN") {
                return 200 "Hello, User from India!";
            }

            return 200 "Hello, User from an unknown country!";
        }
    }
}



